WEBVTT

00:00.860 --> 00:05.470
Angle A is a circumscribed
angle on circle O.

00:05.470 --> 00:07.950
So this is angle
A right over here.

00:07.950 --> 00:11.360
Then when they say it's
a circumscribed angle,

00:11.360 --> 00:13.550
that means that the
two sides of the angle

00:13.550 --> 00:15.820
are tangent to the circle.

00:15.820 --> 00:18.530
So AC is tangent to
the circle at point

00:18.530 --> 00:23.090
C. AB is tangent to
the circle at point B.

00:23.090 --> 00:25.440
What is the measure of angle A?

00:25.440 --> 00:28.730
Now, I encourage you
to pause the video now

00:28.730 --> 00:30.840
and to try this out on your own.

00:30.840 --> 00:32.600
And I'll give you a hint.

00:32.600 --> 00:35.960
It will leverage the fact that
this is a circumscribed angle

00:35.960 --> 00:38.580
as you could imagine.

00:38.580 --> 00:41.140
So I'm assuming you've
given a go at it.

00:41.140 --> 00:42.560
So the other piece
of information

00:42.560 --> 00:45.490
they give us is that angle D,
which is an inscribed angle,

00:45.490 --> 00:50.960
is 48 degrees and it intercepts
the same arc-- so this

00:50.960 --> 00:53.940
is the arc that it intercepts,
arc CB I guess you could call

00:53.940 --> 00:56.640
it-- it intercepts this
arc right over here.

00:56.640 --> 00:57.740
It's the inscribed angle.

00:57.740 --> 01:02.320
The central angle that
intersects that same arc

01:02.320 --> 01:04.840
is going to be twice
the inscribed angle.

01:04.840 --> 01:07.235
So this is going
to be 96 degrees.

01:07.235 --> 01:09.610
I could put three markers here
just because we've already

01:09.610 --> 01:11.370
used the double marker.

01:11.370 --> 01:15.855
Notice, they both intercept
arc CB so some people would

01:15.855 --> 01:18.530
say the measure of
arc CB is 96 degrees,

01:18.530 --> 01:21.180
the central angle is 96
degrees, the inscribed angle

01:21.180 --> 01:23.570
is going to be half
of that, 48 degrees.

01:23.570 --> 01:25.850
So how does this help us?

01:25.850 --> 01:29.560
Well, a key clue is that angle
is a circumscribed angle.

01:29.560 --> 01:34.410
So that means AC and AB are
each tangent to the circle.

01:34.410 --> 01:37.450
Well, a line that is
tangent to the circle

01:37.450 --> 01:40.830
is going to be perpendicular to
the radius of the circle that

01:40.830 --> 01:44.570
intersects the circle
at the same point.

01:44.570 --> 01:49.930
So this right over here is
going to be a 90-degree angle,

01:49.930 --> 01:53.730
and this right over here is
going to be a 90-degree angle.

01:53.730 --> 01:56.380
OC is perpendicular to CA.

01:56.380 --> 02:00.330
OB, which is a radius,
is perpendicular to BA,

02:00.330 --> 02:03.160
which is a tangent line, and
they both intersect right

02:03.160 --> 02:06.520
over here at B. Now, this
might jump out at you.

02:06.520 --> 02:08.509
We have a quadrilateral
going on here.

02:08.509 --> 02:13.480
ABOC is a quadrilateral,
so its sides

02:13.480 --> 02:20.310
are going to add
up to 360 degrees.

02:20.310 --> 02:23.170
So we could know, we
could write it this way.

02:23.170 --> 02:26.380
We could write the
measure of angle A

02:26.380 --> 02:37.930
plus 90 degrees plus another
90 degrees plus 96 degrees

02:37.930 --> 02:40.880
is going to be equal
to 360 degrees.

02:46.620 --> 02:49.720
Or another way of thinking
about it, if we subtract 180

02:49.720 --> 02:52.670
from both sides, if we
subtract that from both sides,

02:52.670 --> 02:59.870
we get the measure of
angle A plus 96 degrees

02:59.870 --> 03:05.142
is going to be equal
to 180 degrees.

03:05.142 --> 03:06.600
Or another way of
thinking about it

03:06.600 --> 03:09.950
is the measure of angle A
or that angle A and angle O

03:09.950 --> 03:12.860
right over here-- you
could call it angle COB--

03:12.860 --> 03:15.620
that these are going to be
supplementary angles if they

03:15.620 --> 03:18.990
add up to 180 degrees.

03:18.990 --> 03:22.130
So if we subtract 96
degrees from both sides,

03:22.130 --> 03:27.561
we get the measure
of angle A is equal

03:27.561 --> 03:30.060
to-- I don't want to make that
look like a less than symbol,

03:30.060 --> 03:32.380
let make it-- measure of
angle-- this one actually

03:32.380 --> 03:35.010
looks more like a--
measure of angle A

03:35.010 --> 03:37.980
is equal to 180 minus 96.

03:37.980 --> 03:39.840
Let's see, 180 minus
90 would be 90,

03:39.840 --> 03:46.190
and then we subtract another
6 gets us to 84 degrees.
